# ── EchoOrchestrator environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env and fill in real values.
#
# This file carries what the *containers* need, not what the applications
# need. Every service reads its own settings from the NocoDB base
# `IdentityBase`, table `auth_tbl_Settings` — the OAuth and UISP credentials,
# the database coordinates each app connects with, the public URLs, and
# `trustedCIDR`, which is one value the whole platform shares rather than a
# differently-named CIDR per service. See localsplash/identity#15.
#
# The base is found by NAME at runtime, never by a base ID: a pasted ID
# survives a rename and outlives a restore. The name is expected to be unique
# — NocoDB does not enforce that, we do.

# ── The settings store (NocoDB at nocodb.X.TLD) ──────────────────────────────
# Every service gets exactly these two. Generate the token in the NocoDB UI:
# Account → Tokens. A service that cannot find IdentityBase retries once at
# startup and then exits saying so — there is no fallback.
NOCODB_BASE_URL=http://nocodb:8080
NOCODB_API_TOKEN=generate-in-nocodb-ui

# ── MySQL (EchoDatabase) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The database container configures itself from these — it cannot read its
# own credentials out of a settings table it is hosting. The applications get
# their DB_* coordinates from auth_tbl_Settings instead.
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-me-root
MYSQL_DATABASE=echo_db
MYSQL_USER=echo_app
MYSQL_PASSWORD=change-me-app
